<title>UK: Quebec sets $200 million seven-year FRN. [CORRECTED 22:25 GMT]</title>
<headline>Quebec sets $200 million seven-year FRN. [CORRECTED 22:25 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quebec has settled (corrects from launched) a $200 million seven-year FRN paying three-month LIBOR plus 15 basis points, sole manager Lehman Brothers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The London-listed deal, privately issued under an EMTN (European medium-term note) programme, is available in denominations of $100,000 and matures in June 2004.</p>
<p>(Corrects to add that the deal is privately issued under an EMTN programme.)</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
